WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.926
If a dishwasher problem survives one conversation the evidence should

00:00:03.926 --> 00:00:09.027
too FixProof keeps the symptom the source and the user's confirmed outcomes

00:00:09.027 --> 00:00:11.704
together Here's the current four-model build

00:00:12.772 --> 00:00:17.079
I'll start a fictional drying case and ask what to check first FixProof

00:00:17.079 --> 00:00:21.262
suggests waiting for drying to finish then links directly to page forty-one

00:00:21.262 --> 00:00:26.126
of the manufacturer's manual The model chooses a bounded check The application

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.958
owns the instruction and citation

00:00:28.974 --> 00:00:33.162
Here's the key rule A suggestion is not evidence that someone performed

00:00:33.162 --> 00:00:37.749
a check The user records what actually happened In this fictional case

00:00:37.999 --> 00:00:42.424
the glasses remain wet after thirty minutes That outcome is saved but

00:00:42.424 --> 00:00:44.262
the problem is not declared fixed

00:00:45.296 --> 00:00:50.234
Now reload and resume The observation is still here Ask what to check

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:54.120
next and FixProof moves to rinse aid instead of repeating the recorded

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.016
check The case changes the next interaction

00:00:58.042 --> 00:01:01.704
The current release covers ten issue paths for three exact Bosch models

00:01:02.017 --> 00:01:06.030
and eight separately mapped paths for one Electrolux model Each uses

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:10.380
its own manufacturer's manual Unsupported model and issue combinations

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.092
stop without a suggested check

00:01:13.116 --> 00:01:17.478
The handover carries the exact model the recorded outcome the observation

00:01:17.641 --> 00:01:22.104
and the source page It also states what is still unknown Someone can

00:01:22.104 --> 00:01:25.491
pick up the case without treating an assistant's suggestion as a fact

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:31.175
We tested that handover format not customer outcomes Across fifty-four

00:01:31.175 --> 00:01:35.234
blind reads by three local model families structured handovers recovered

00:01:35.235 --> 00:01:38.564
two hundred fifty-four of two hundred seventy fields with zero critical

00:01:38.564 --> 00:01:42.635
errors Equal-fact transcripts recovered two hundred forty-three with

00:01:42.636 --> 00:01:47.066
five critical errors Results varied by case and the complete synthetic

00:01:47.066 --> 00:01:48.131
evidence is public

00:01:49.168 --> 00:01:53.593
If a burning smell is reported troubleshooting stops The pending check

00:01:53.593 --> 00:01:58.168
disappears the warning remains after reload and the original report stays

00:01:58.168 --> 00:02:01.193
in the handover No diagnosis is invented

00:02:02.226 --> 00:02:06.657
Judges can call the public M C P endpoint directly An official client

00:02:06.657 --> 00:02:10.382
discovered five tools read a fictional outcome across new connections

00:02:10.691 --> 00:02:14.516
and found that the recorded check was not repeated The handover also

00:02:14.516 --> 00:02:19.021
advertises a self-contained M C P App The complete trace and live proof

00:02:19.021 --> 00:02:20.073
are linked from the site

00:02:21.092 --> 00:02:25.688
FixProof has not run on an Alexa device or proven a repair outcome It

00:02:25.688 --> 00:02:29.880
demonstrates a narrower result across four exact models a stateful assistant

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:33.213
can carry user-confirmed observations and their sources into the next

00:02:33.213 --> 00:02:37.708
conversation Try the live M C P workflow or the browser simulation
